      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T14:17:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@peter, if you\u0027re checking the coordclampshader against a \"closest positive\", it won\u0027t be a graphite-generated image. Graphite hasn\u0027t wired up anisotropic filtering, so comparing to a config other than `grmtl` or `grdawnmtl` will highlight differences from that in addition to any changes from this optimization.\n\nI only see changes to the top-left clamped image when sticking with Graphite configs",
      "parentUuid": "4403c448_e6729cb7",
      "revId": "49a6112bb9a4f26e863fb0ba267dc6f8b5a716f9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2468321c_a987ca9b",
