      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T15:24:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `rsx_blob_shader` changes are also a bug that requires another check unfortunately. Right now the KeyContext\u0027s \"local2Dev\" transform is initialized from the transform stored on the `DrawParams` object that\u0027s recorded and eventually processed when creating a DrawPass.\n\nFor shapes and tessellated paths, this transform is always the full local-to-device transform, but I hadn\u0027t realized that for coverage masks (atlases, and text, etc.) the full transform is often decomposed into a part that\u0027s embedded into the shape drawn in the mask, and then a remaining post-mask transform. The post-mask transform is what\u0027s stored in the DrawParams, and each mask-ish Geometry type has its own way of reconstructing the correct true local coordinates for shaders.\n\nUnfortunately in these cases that means the KeyContext\u0027s \"local2Dev\" matrix isn\u0027t seeing the whole thing, and often sees just an integer translation matrix instead. In `rsx_blob_shader` case, there\u0027s a 1.4 scale factor that\u0027s been embedded in the glyph masks and then the text renderstep is further scaling the local coords to compensate, but KeyHelpers is now thinking it can switch to nearest.  The underlying the rectangle fill sees the whole transform correctly and doesn\u0027t switch to nearest.",
      "parentUuid": "32569505_976b57f2",
      "revId": "49a6112bb9a4f26e863fb0ba267dc6f8b5a716f9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96113ecc_8d9d1702",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T15:25:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am hoping to be able to move uniform and paint key extraction to be at the time the draw is called, which would mean the full transform is always available to set on the KeyContext, so we wouldn\u0027t run into the issue of reconstructing an incomplete transform from a RenderStep that decomposed it.",
      "parentUuid": "2468321c_a987ca9b",
      "revId": "49a6112bb9a4f26e863fb0ba267dc6f8b5a716f9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65539194_9532c0a9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T15:32:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A short term fix that shouldn\u0027t be too hard, that should catch the coordclampshader and rsx_blob_shader issues would be to add a value to `KeyContext::Scope` like `kSkipSamplingOptimizations`.\n\nIn the `add_to_key` function for `SkCoordClampShader`, it would pass in a KeyContextWithScope that switches to `kSkipSamplingOptimizations` if it\u0027s not `kDefault`. In `ContextUtils::ExtractPaintData`, we\u0027d add a new parameter to take the initial scope for the KeyContext. If the DrawParams\u0027 geometry is a Shape, we use kDefault. If it\u0027s anything else, we use kSkipSamplingOptimizations.",
      "parentUuid": "96113ecc_8d9d1702",
      "revId": "49a6112bb9a4f26e863fb0ba267dc6f8b5a716f9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
